#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cascadia-web -- a web browser for the iPad 2's touch screen, whose videos
play in mpv (tools/desktop/web-setup.sh installs it).

  cascadia-web [URL | WORDS...]

Pages render in WebKitGTK; videos do not.  hook.js, in every frame, stops a
video the moment it starts and hands what it knows of it here, and the
browser gives it to cascadia-play: mpv, as the YouTube tool plays, with the
stream yt-dlp finds that this iPad decodes in real time.  When the player
closes, the page is where it was.  Started by a tap only: a page cannot start
the player by itself, and videos that play by themselves stay stopped.

For the iPad's two A9 cores and 512 MB:
  - a phone's user agent (menu: Desktop site): sites send their lighter
    mobile pages.  Chrome's, on Android: WebKitGTK plays no HLS by its
    address, and players that see Safari or an iPhone give it just that,
    where for Chrome they feed Media Source -- which works here
  - ads blocked at the network (menu: Block ads): a list of ad servers that
    web-setup.sh fetches, compiled by WebKit once
  - pages drawn on the CPU, not through the GPU: as fast, steadier and ~50 MB
    lighter (setup_webkit has the numbers; CASCADIA_WEB_GPU=1 for the GPU)
  - while mpv starts and plays, the browser's page processes are stopped and
    their memory goes out to swap, the browser's own and the warm yt-dlp's
    once it plays, and zram's writeback to the NAND waits (cascadia-play
    --freeze and --page-out; it lets them go even if this browser dies)
  - yt-dlp kept warm (cascadia-ytdl), from a few seconds after the start: a
    video starts ~10 s sooner
  - JavaScript ~2.3 times as fast with the ARMv7 build of WebKit, when
    web-setup.sh could fetch the one that matches (the launcher picks it)
Touch: big buttons; the on-screen keyboard comes up for a text field you tap
(menu to turn that off) and with the keyboard button; tabs only when a page
opens one; hold a link for "Play in the video player".

Kept in ~/.config/cascadia-web (settings, the start page's tiles),
~/.local/share/cascadia-web (cookies, site data) and ~/.cache/cascadia-web.
"""
